what's up  reject nation greg alba here thank you  so much for clicking on this video  means a lot to have you here today so i  actually have something  very personal and very exciting to share  with all of you today if you've been  following me on youtube for a while now  it's pretty apparent my main passion  it's in movies and you might have heard  me say this before but specifically  my main drive is actually in  screenwriting and now  i might just be able to turn that dream  into a reality see when we started this  channel initially it was meant to just  be a stepping stone i didn't think it  would actually be a major part of my  career pursuits and of course  none of the success we've had would be  possible without your support which i'm  forever grateful for because after  several years  i still love making videos and the  channel's not going away anytime soon  however i never lost sight of my actual  goal  which was to one day graduate from you  know just  talking about movies and actually making  movies  now how did i finally get to this point  a couple years ago i became friends with  joel harlow he's an academy award winner  a key makeup and special effects artist  who's worked on such films like the  pirates of the caribbean trilogy  black panther the star trek films  logan a whole bunch of movies and shows  too many  name right now but for sure you've seen  his work in fact he was on this channel  once before  the biggest accomplishment out of his  whole career he uh reached out to me  about developing an idea of his  and turning it into a feature film  within the horror genre and of course  i said yes i mean i mean why wouldn't i  i mean he's the key makeup artist for i  love you philip morris fortunately  the whole team behind it is cool with me  talking about it right here on the  channel so i wanted to give you guys a  first look  at who's involved and what we've got  cooking for a new horror anthology  called old time radio i can't believe  i'm finally talking about this it's  going to have three full original  stories as well as a wrap around tale  that ties it together the script's  already been written and if you guys  want a taste for what we have in store  we just launched our official website  called oldtimerradiohorror.net  there you'll find story details and  concept art for our three  sinister tales some behind the scenes  images and videos as well as a proof of  concept short film introducing you  to the film's wraparound tale the latter  of which i  highly encourage you to go check out the  movie was written by  yours truly my buddy patrick hogue whose  horror short film called so you might  have seen on crypt tv  and joel harlow himself producer lloyd  levin is currently working with us and i  think i'm saying his name right i really  ought to know if i'm saying his name  right i should have fact checked that  11. he's produced the watchmen movie and  series the hellboy franchise and one of  my all-time favorite movies  boogie nights this film is like a  spiritual sequel to boogie night it's  not  basically with this movie what we want  to do is give a fresh spin  on a horror anthology merge it with the  atmospheric elements of a classic radio  horror drama while also delivering an  original film  with nuanced characters and of course  keeping it scary so  if you want a glimpse into the morbidly  nostalgic world that we've created i put  a link in the description box and pinned  comment to the short film that's  inspired by the wraparound tale the  story takes place on halloween evening  where decrepit housemates rick kissgrim  and edward  d mize engage in their annual tradition  feverishly awaiting a new trio of tales  from their possessed  old time radio so how it works in the  movie every time we drift into the  glowing dial of the crossley cathedral  radio the voice of our host  introduces another horror tale  can you count how many times i've said  horror  in this video did you guys know it was a  horror film oh yeah i should have  mentioned this earlier  but you know the segway is just too good  of an opportunity to pass up the host is  being played by none other  than paul giamatti that is not dream  casting  that is real we told him it was sideways  too but back to the actual movie  pat patrick i call him pat pat wrote the  first anthology tale  scarecrow i wrote the other two which  are titled live bait and chicken heart  like i've mentioned it's inspired by the  vintage horror radio classics of  yesteryear but in all honesty it serves  as more than just a trip down nostalgia  lane each story's focused on characters  and plot are  very different from one another they  each have its own unique tones  themes and just overall flavor can't  even say they're all the same kind of  horror you can go to the website to read  through the plot and story details and  check out some awesome  concept art that we have all that fun  stuff anyway i could  spend all night telling you guys about  all the details but i'll end it with  this  if you've made it this far first off  thank you for listening  everything i have talked about is all  linked in the description box and pinned  comment  for you boys and girls for the reject  nation to go ahead and check out we've  been working hard  you gotta walk hard we've been working  very hard and diligently  and i really can't wait for old time  radio to be brought to life and for you  guys to be a part of the journey all i  really ask is that you cruise the site  and if you like what you see  leave a comment or if just hearing me  talk about this is making you want to  see this film  leave a comment here or on the short  film engagement algorithm it all helps  sincerely i mean it if it wasn't for all  the support you've shown me over the  years  i wouldn't have the confidence to go out  and achieve the next steps and take some  chances  so in all sincerity i wouldn't be here  talking about any of this if it wasn't  for all of you  thank you again and  go check out the goddamn website

